82\nLocation: 18 FR 3777, PDF pages 1-2 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 1 of 16 ===\nREGISTER\nVOLUME 18 19344 U n ited %\nWashington, Thursday, July 2, 1953\nNUMBER 128\nTITLE 3— THE PRESIDENT\nEXECUTIVE ORDER 10465\nS u spe n sio n op  Certain  P rovisions  op  the  \nO fficer  P ersonnel  A ct of  1947, as \nA m ended, W h ic h R elate  to O fficers  \nof  the  M arine  C orps\nBy virtue of the authority vested in \nme by section 426 (c) of the Officer Per­\nsonnel Act of 1947, as amended by sec­\ntion 1  (h) of the act of June 30, 1951, \n65 Stat. 109, it is ordered as follows:\n1 . The operation of those provisions \nof Title III of the Officer Personnel Act \nof 1947, as amended, which relate to the \ndistribution in grades, promotion by se­\nlection, temporary promotion, and dis­\ncharge on second failure of selection for \npromotion, of officers of the Marine \nCorps of the grades of major, captain, \nfirst lieutenant, and second lieutenant \nis hereby suspended until June 30 of the \nfiscal year following that in which the \nnational emergency proclaimed by Proc­\nlamation No. 2914 of Dece","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_10467.txt","sha256":"fff6d757c83af60362f9949d6d435857266e1921f2ae49966b9850162f1f8307","source":{"line":767,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"cc2d0e7d1a175fe9ddd276e4bff1213fa05f6254106434e67d9b091d6bdd3e81"}}]}
